      <div type="clause" n="23.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 23.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="162" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ofga ælc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.11"/> mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.4"/> his tihtlan mid foreaðe, swa we ær cwædon; ⁊ beo þæra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.11"/> ælc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.11"/> fæstende<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.11"/> on ægþera<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.18"/> hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.4"/> se ðær mid sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.3"/>, (on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.14"/>) Godes bebode ⁊ ðæs ærcebiscopes; ⁊ ne beo ðær on naþre healf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1-2"/> (na<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.2"/>) ma monna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.3"/> þonne XII. Gif se getihtloda mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.3"/> ðonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.4"/> maran werude<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.5"/> beo þonne twelfa sum, þonne beo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.6"/> þæt ordal forod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.7"/>, buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.3"/> hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.8"/> him from<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.3"/> gan willon.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23.2" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="162" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ofga ylc man his tyhtan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1"/> mid foreaþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1"/>, swa we ær cwædon; ⁊ beo ðæra ylc fæstende on ægþere hand ðe ðær sy, be Godes bebode ⁊ ðæs bisceopes; ⁊ ne beo ðær on nawþre healfa ma manne ðonne XII. Gif ðonne se getyhtleda man maran weorod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1"/> sy þonne XII sum, ðonne sy þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ordale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1"/> forode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1"/>, buton hi him fram gán wille.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23.2" corresp="#wit-ot"><pb n="162" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ofga ælc m<hi rend="italic">an</hi> his . . . mid foreaþe, swa we ær cwædon; ⁊ beo ðara ælc fæst . . . hand þe ðær mid sie, Godes bebode ⁊ þæs ærcebisc . . .; . . on nauþre healfe ma manna ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> XII. Gif se ge . . . :on<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> maran weorode sie ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> XII su<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> sie þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> or . . ., . . hie hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> fra<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gan willen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="23.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="163" ed="#liebermann"/>Et prosequatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.36"/> omnis homo compellationem suam preiuramento<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.37"/>, sicut supra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.38"/> dictum est. Et sint utrimque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.39"/> ieiuni, ex precepto Dei et archiepiscopi, et non sint in alterutra parte amplius quam in alia et hoc sit utrimque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.40"/> XII homines. Si uero<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.41"/> (autem) accusatus homo maiorem defensionem habeat quam XII hominum, sit ipsum ordalium in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1-3"/> eo fractum, nisi recedere uelint ab eo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.2-2"/> (illo).<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="23.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="140" ed="#attenborough"/>⁊ ofga ælc mon his tihtlan mid foreaðe<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.4"/>, swa we ær cwædon; ⁊ beo þæra ælc fæstende on ægþera<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.5"/> hond se<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.6"/> ðær mid sy, on<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.7"/> Godes bebode ⁊ ðæs ærcebiscopes<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.8"/>; ⁊ ne beo ðær on naþre healf<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.9"/> na ma monna þonne XII. Gif se getihtloda mon ðonne maran werude beo<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.10"/> þonne twelfa sum, þonne beo þæt ordal forod<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.11"/>, buton hy him from gan willon<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.12"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="163" ed="#liebermann"/>Und jedermann erreiche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.1"/> seine Klage [zwinge Verklagten zum Beweise] durch [seinen] Voreid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.2"/>, wie wir zuvor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.3"/> bestimmt haben; und es faste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.4"/> auf beiden Seiten jeder von ihnen, der dabei steht, laut Gottes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.5"/> und des Erzbischofs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.6"/> Gebot; und es sei da auf keiner Seite mehr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.4"/> an Männern [anwesend] als [je] 12. Wenn der verklagte Mann aber von grösserer Männerschaar [begleitet] ist als selbzwölft, so sei dann dies Ordal gescheitert<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.7"/>, es sei denn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.8"/>, sie [die mehr als 12] wollen von ihm fortgehen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.9"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let everyone pursue his charge [compel the accused to proof] by [his] fore-oath, as we determined before; and on both sides let each of those who stand there fast, by the command of God and of the archbishop; and let there be no more men [present] on either side than 12 [each]. But if the accused man is [accompanied] by a larger band of men than himself and eleven others, then let the ordeal be void, unless they [those over 12] are willing to leave him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="141" ed="#attenborough"/>And every man shall precede his accusation with an oath, as we have already declared<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.n.1"/>, and everyone who is present in both parties shall fast according to the command of God and the archbishop. And there shall not be more than twelve on either side. If, however, the accused man is one of a party greater than twelve, the ordeal shall be invalidated, unless they<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_23-2.attnote.n.2"/> will leave him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="422" ed="#whitelock"/>And each man is to obtain [the right to pursue] his charge by a preliminary oath, as we have said before; and each of those of both parties who is present is to be fasting, according to the command of God and of the archbishop; and there are not to be on either side more men than twelve. If the accused man then is one of a larger company than twelve,<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_23-2.whinote.n.1"/> the ordeal is then invalidated, unless they will leave him.</ab>
