        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.39" n="39" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">utrique <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">utrique MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.40" n="40" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> utrobique <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; utrobique the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.41" n="41" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> a. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. Lond; a. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> f. in eo <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; f. in eo the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eo <hi rend="italic">Lond T;</hi> illo <hi rend="italic">RMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eo Lond T; illo RMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hier schiebt R ein:</hi> De ordalio (<hi rend="italic">Schmids App.</hi> XVI)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">here R inserts: De ordalio (Schmid's App. XVI)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘beginne’, sondern ‘erlange’. Der Klageeid (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 14) steht nicht immer zu Beginn des Prozesses</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘begin’, but ‘obtain’. The plaintiff’s oath (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 14) does not always stand at the beginning of the proceedings</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wahrscheinlich hierher, und zwar aus dem Ags., Hn 64, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hn 64, 1 probably belongs here, deriving indeed from the A.-S.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die von Schmid p. <hi rend="smallcaps">xliv</hi> zitierten Stellen 9. 11 sind die einzigen, die Klageeid erwähnen. Aber sie beziehen sich auf die zwei Sonderfälle des Anefangs und der Anschuldigung, dass ein als Verbrecher Getöteter nur fälschlich als Verbrecher behandelt sei. Das Zitat scheint vielmehr ein allgemeines Gesetz zu meinen; dies wäre dann verloren; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The passages 9. 11 cited by Schmid p. <hi rend="smallcaps">xliv</hi> are the only ones that mention the plaintiff’s oath. But they relate to the two special cases of attachment and of the charge that a man slain as a criminal had only been wrongly treated as a criminal. The citation seems rather to refer to a general law; this would then be lost; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Ordal 14. a; Fasten 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Ordal 14. a; Fasten 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dies klingt vielleicht an den Eingang jenes <hi rend="italic">Ordal</hi> (<hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 23, 1⁴) 1 an: <hi rend="italic">Godes bebodum ⁊ þæs arcebiscopes</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This perhaps echoes the opening of that <hi rend="italic">Ordal</hi> (<hi rend="italic">above</hi> 23, 1⁴) 1: <hi rend="italic">Godes bebodum ⁊ þæs arcebiscopes</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Gott und Erzbischof’ bed. Einen Begriff: ‘Kirche’; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> Einl. 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘God and archbishop’ means a single concept: ‘church’; see above Introduction 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Kläger erscheint also mit 11, und das bed. hier selbzwölft; so auch Wülfing in <hi rend="italic">Engl. Stud.</hi> 24, 463. — Die Worte <hi rend="italic">beo þæt ordal forod,</hi> wegen Ungleichheit der Zahl der Parteien, kehren wieder Ordal 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The plaintiff thus appears with 11, and that is what ‘himself the twelfth’ means here; so too Wülfing in <hi rend="italic">Engl. Stud.</hi> 24, 463. — The words <hi rend="italic">beo þæt ordal forod,</hi> on account of inequality in the number of the parties, recur in Ordal 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso heisst es: Verteidiger des Verbrechers verwirken den Frieden, <hi rend="italic">buton hig him fram gan willan</hi> VI 8, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Similarly it is said: defenders of the criminal forfeit the peace, <hi rend="italic">buton hig him fram gan willan</hi> VI 8, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier schiebt der Q-Abschreiber R (<hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 21¹) das Stück <hi rend="italic">Ordal</hi> (<hi rend="italic">o.</hi> I 386) ein, offenbar nur des verwandten Inhalts wegen, ohne dass es im Q-Original, geschweige im Archetyp von II As, hier stand</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Here the Q copyist R (see above 21¹) inserts the piece <hi rend="italic">Ordal</hi> (<hi rend="italic">above</hi> I 386), evidently only because of its related content, without its having stood here in the Q original, let alone in the archetype of II As</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Apparently a reference to a lost law.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e</hi>. those in excess of 12 (cf. <hi rend="italic">Dom be hatan isene</hi>, cap. 1 § 4).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>foreaðe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">tyhtan mid foreaþ</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>ægþera</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ægþere</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>se</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðe</hi>. Ld, Ot.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>on</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">be</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>ærcebiscopes</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">bisceopes</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>healf</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Altered to <hi rend="italic">healfe</hi>. <hi rend="italic">nawþre healfa</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>beo</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">weorod sy</hi>. Ld. <hi rend="italic">weorode sie</hi>. Ot.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>forod</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">sy ðæt ordale forode</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>willon</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wille</hi>. Ld. <hi rend="italic">willen</hi>. Ot.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IIAs_23-2.whinote.n.1" n="1" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">422</biblScope></bibl><label>twelve</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">From the ambiguity of the expression <hi rend="italic">twelfa sum</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> p. 159, n. 11), it is uncertain whether this figure is inclusive of the defendant or not.</seg></note>
